Z||000015||Oreif||07-30-2000||10:35 PM||||That Holley Air scoop is rare. I have seen them bring $80 to $150 on Ebay. But I wouldn't buy the Car for $1500.||||reg||1
Z||000016||KES||07-30-2000||10:47 PM||||Thanx Guys   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> To be honest I hadn't been trying to use code or real smiley's.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> call me lazy - guess its an e-mail thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> And I can pull and do engines though not my forte - nor is it desired - just to cheap (read poor) to pay someone to do it. nor do I trust most shops (psychological thing I guess) but ya - i guess a carry over from the y bodies is a desire to keep it original - more from a future collector standpoint I guess - protecting it for the next generation in my mind.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by KES (edited 07-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||theogre||07-30-2000||11:29 PM||||Kes,<BR> <BR>We'd rather you asked now than later like allot of people do.<P>I'd also pass on that one, way too much rust in places hard to fix. <P>I can tell you from personal experience that fixing the top beam of a door because of a snagged mirror is a royal pain. Mine was like that. The thing is better now after some beating on it but that door will be replaced as part of the power window upgrade in order to get it true. If the top beam isn't close to true the window will rattle/bind/leak/etc untill it's fixed.<P>There's a couple red ones down the road from me for sale. At least one's a fast back. Didn't really look at them. (In Wilminton DE area.)<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000018||HYPTNOTiSE||07-31-2000||08:09 AM||||Kevin, i think you should look for an 88GT. I mean you might as well get the most rare year with all the updated good stuff on it. Especially if you get a yellow GT to match your LT-5 powered LS-1 vette. <BR>I envy you for that. Those cars are incredible machines! Let me know if you ever want to put a fiero v-6 in your vette, then you wouldn't need to buy a fiero, you could combine both of your interests/hobbys <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Oh and i'll take that junk Lt-5 and computer and stuff, you wont be needing that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Sound good? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||KES||07-31-2000||12:30 PM||||Damn, I think you guys hit it on the head now.  I really appreciate all this - ogre I think your door story finally convinced me - it's just now sinking in that this "project" would end up being more in time and $ than its worth   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> However as you mentioned (hypno) the dream Fiero would be an 88 Yellow GT for excactly the reason you mentioned. Yes, the ZR-1 is/was an amazing vehicle. The Lt-5 is a phenominal engine - I never dreamed to own one - it was definately a blessing to have this opportunity.  I know this is a fiero board but since it was brought up. My yellow is one of 11 93 Yellow Zr1's made.  I drove a 90 at watkins glenn a couple years back and these things just sing when they get the chance. However - the LS-1 is no slouch and the new LS-6 should be watched closely.  There will be more power coming in the next few years.<P>------------------<BR>Kevin Silva<BR>1993 ZR1 #307-Competition Yellow/Black<BR>1999 Ram 3500 4x4 QC-TurboDiesel<BR>NCM - #4738 <P><p>[This message has been edited by KES (edited 07-31-2000).]||||reg||12
